{"id": "2026-09-09-news-us-strikes-iranian-tankers-iran-hits-jordan-base", "date": "2026-09-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "US strikes Iranian tankers; Iran hits Jordan base", "summary": "The US destroyed five Iranian oil tankers; Iran fired ~20 ballistic missiles at a US base in Jordan, most intercepted, as crude passed $100.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/us-strikes-oil-tankers-off-coast-of-iran/a-79194562", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "security"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "The United States struck five Iranian oil tankers on Tuesday 8 September, and Iran retaliated overnight by firing some 20 ballistic missiles at a US military base in Jordan — 18 of which Jordan's air force said it intercepted early Wednesday 9 September. [ongoing since 2026-09-05]. US Central Command (CENTCOM — the US military's Middle East headquarters) said it hit four tankers in the Gulf of Oman (the Kaviz, Charminar, Horizon 1 and Riesco) and one, the Derya, near Kharg Island off the Strait of Hormuz — the narrow Gulf chokepoint through which roughly a fifth of the world's seaborne oil passes — after the IRGC (Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps, Iran's elite military branch) twice targeted a US Navy warship with ballistic missiles. CENTCOM said crews were ordered to abandon ship beforehand and reported no casualties, and cast the vessels as a \"multibillion-dollar shadow network\" funding Iran's proxies — its own characterisation, not an independently verified finding. Jordan, a US ally that hosts an American base, said 20 missiles were fired toward its territory and two fell in unpopulated areas; a US official called the strike ineffective, with all personnel accounted for. The IRGC said it hit two US ships, eight tankers and 10 other \"non-compliant\" vessels in the Strait, and warned tankers off Bahrain and Kuwait to leave or be targeted; oil rose above $100 a barrel for the first time in nearly six weeks.", "why": "the first Iranian missile strike on Jordanian soil widens a naval war that had been largely confined to the Gulf's shipping lanes, and the threat to tankers off Kuwait and Bahrain — with crude back over $100 — signals the disruption is spreading from Iran's own exports toward the wider Gulf supply that Europe partly depends on.", "thread_id": "2026-09-06-news-us-strikes-iranian-tankers-irgc-hits-back", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-06", "event_date": "2026-09-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United States", "Iran", "IRGC", "Strait of Hormuz", "Jordan"]}
{"id": "2026-09-09-news-eleven-states-join-uk-settlement-goods-ban", "date": "2026-09-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Eleven states join UK settlement-goods ban", "summary": "After Britain banned settlement-goods imports, 11 more countries announced they will move to restrict trade with Israeli West Bank settlements.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/9/which-countries-banned-goods-from-settlements-but-trade-with-israel", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Eleven more countries said they will move to restrict trade with Israeli West Bank settlements, after Britain formally banned settlement-goods imports in a statement Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband gave to Parliament on Tuesday 8 September. [ongoing since 2026-09-08]. In a joint statement issued after Miliband's speech, Canada, Denmark, Finland, France, Iceland, Ireland, Norway, Poland, Portugal, Spain and Sweden backed a two-state solution and signalled their own intended curbs; Spain, Ireland, the Netherlands and Belgium had already announced national bans earlier this year. The UK measure — covering settlement exports such as dates, olive oil and farm produce — is to take effect within six to nine months. Israel reacted furiously, announcing countermeasures that include barring 12 British MPs from entry and closing the British consulate in Jerusalem. The EU is Israel's largest trading partner, taking 31.7% of its goods trade in 2025 (about €43.3bn).", "why": "a coordinated move by a dozen mostly European governments turns months of condemnation over settlement expansion into concrete trade measures — though the practical bite of each depends on national enforcement detail not yet spelled out.", "thread_id": "2026-09-08-news-uk-to-ban-israeli-settlement-goods", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-08", "event_date": "2026-09-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United Kingdom", "Israel", "European Union", "Canada"]}
{"id": "2026-09-09-news-us-bans-canadian-dairy-alcohol-motorcycles", "date": "2026-09-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "US bans Canadian dairy, alcohol, motorcycles", "summary": "The White House will ban imports of Canadian dairy, most alcohol and some motorcycles and add 50% tariffs on more goods after Canada's retaliation.", "url": "https://apnews.com/article/canada-carney-trump-tariffs-trade-war-a5fbb50d1c30327ae813482556a37ac3", "source_domain": "apnews.com", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["ongoing"], "topics": ["economy", "geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The White House said on Tuesday 8 September it will ban imports of Canadian dairy, most alcohol and some motorcycles and impose fresh 50% tariffs on other goods — a day after Canada's retaliatory tariffs took effect. [ongoing since 2026-08-22]. The import ban is set to start on 29 September; the 50% tariffs on additional goods — mattresses, motorboats and golf carts — begin 15 September. It answers Canada's Monday 7 September move to put retaliatory tariffs of up to 50% on about $20 billion of US goods, itself a response to the 50% US tariffs imposed in August. The White House said the alcohol ban partly retaliates for Canadian provinces pulling US wines and spirits from shelves, which President Trump called \"discriminatory.\" Prime Minister Mark Carney said Canada would accelerate efforts to cut its reliance on the US: \"It's about ensuring that no country can hold us hostage.\"", "why": "two of the world's most integrated economies — nearly 68% of Canadian exports go to the US — are now trading outright import bans, casting doubt over the USMCA free-trade pact and pushing Ottawa toward closer ties with the EU.", "thread_id": "2026-08-22-weekend-us-imposes-50-tariffs-on-canadian-goods", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-22", "event_date": "2026-09-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United States", "Canada", "Donald Trump", "Mark Carney"]}
{"id": "2026-09-09-news-netanyahu-denies-pre-oct-7-uae-warning", "date": "2026-09-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Netanyahu denies pre-Oct 7 UAE warning", "summary": "Netanyahu denied a book's claim that the UAE warned him 10 days before 7 October 2023 that Hamas was planning a major attack.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/israel-s-netanyahu-denies-uae-warned-him-of-october-7-attack/a-79194436", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["disputed"], "topics": ["politics", "geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Tuesday 8 September denied a report that the United Arab Emirates warned him, ten days before the 7 October 2023 Hamas attack, that the group was planning a major operation. [disputed]. The claim comes from a book excerpt by two journalists at the left-leaning daily Haaretz, which says UAE President Mohammed bin Zayed told Netanyahu that Hamas and its Gaza leader Yahya Sinwar were preparing a large assault that could derail the Abraham Accords — the 2020 US-brokered deals normalising relations between Israel and several Arab states. Netanyahu allegedly reacted with \"relative calm,\" replying that an attack was likelier to come from the West Bank. His office said \"no warning was given,\" while the UAE neither confirmed nor denied the account, saying relevant intelligence \"has been and continues to be communicated\"; The Times of Israel reported the same story, citing an Emirati source.", "why": "with Israeli elections due next month (October), the report sharpens a fight over who bears responsibility for the 7 October intelligence failure — opposition figure and former military chief Gadi Eisenkot said the signs increasingly show Netanyahu \"blindly led Israel into the disaster\" — even as the core claim rests on a single, contested book account that the prime minister rejects.", "thread_id": "2026-09-09-news-netanyahu-denies-pre-oct-7-uae-warning", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-09", "event_date": "2026-09-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Benjamin Netanyahu", "Israel", "United Arab Emirates", "Hamas"]}
{"id": "2026-09-09-news-ukraine-hits-novorossiysk-moldova-border-struck", "date": "2026-09-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Ukraine hits Novorossiysk; Moldova border struck", "summary": "Ukraine struck the Russian Black Sea port of Novorossiysk, killing four; Russian drones hit a Ukraine-Moldova crossing, killing two.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/live/2026/09/09/en-direct-guerre-en-ukraine-kiev-revendique-une-attaque-d-ampleur-contre-la-base-navale-russe-de-novorossiisk-en-mer-noire_6766818_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Ukraine struck the Russian Black Sea port of Novorossiysk overnight into Wednesday 9 September, killing at least four people including a child, while Russian drones hit a crossing on the Ukraine–Moldova border, killing two. [ongoing since 2026-08-25]. Russia's Krasnodar governor said 29 people were wounded at Novorossiysk — a major outlet for Russian oil and grain exports — and that nearly 600 Ukrainian drones were shot down overnight. Ukraine said the Starokozace crossing on the Moldovan border, about 500 km south of Kyiv, was hit and forced to close; Moldova's president Maia Sandu warned that \"Russia's frontline is moving west.\" The exchange came a day after Russia resumed near-daily strikes on Kyiv following the inconclusive Witkoff–Kushner mission to Moscow, and after a Putin–Trump phone call that the Kremlin called \"extremely frank.\"", "why": "strikes on a Moldovan-border crossing and a key Russian export port show the war spilling outward even as US-brokered talks stall, with both capitals bracing for a third winter of full-scale fighting.", "thread_id": "2026-08-26-news-ukraine-strikes-stall-russian-grain-exports", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-26", "event_date": "2026-09-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Russia", "Novorossiysk", "Moldova"]}
{"id": "2026-09-09-news-swiss-solar-tops-hydro-storage-in-july", "date": "2026-09-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss solar tops hydro storage in July", "summary": "For the first time, Swiss photovoltaic output exceeded accumulation-hydro output in a single month (July 2026), after a dry summer.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/surprise-au-pays-des-barrages-cet-ete-le-solaire-a-commence-a-chatouiller-l-hydraulique-en-suisse", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Swiss solar panels out-produced the country's hydropower reservoirs in a single month for the first time in July 2026, Le Temps reported, as a dry, sunny summer reshaped the national power mix. [single-source]. Photovoltaic (solar) generation exceeded the output of accumulation plants — the dammed Alpine reservoirs that store water to generate electricity on demand — for the first time that month, a notable marker in a country whose power system has been anchored by hydro for a century. The dry summer cut reservoir inflows while sunny weather lifted solar yields.", "why": "solar's rapid build-out is beginning to rival the technology that has defined Swiss electricity for generations, with consequences for how the grid is balanced and, above all, for winter supply, when solar fades and reservoir water matters most.", "thread_id": "2026-09-09-news-swiss-solar-tops-hydro-storage-in-july", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-09", "event_date": "2026-07-31", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland"]}
{"id": "2026-09-09-news-87-of-swiss-back-youth-social-media-ban", "date": "2026-09-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "87% of Swiss back youth social-media ban", "summary": "A survey of 8,317 people found 87% in Switzerland support banning social media for minors, citing mental-health risks.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/87-de-la-population-suisse-veut-interdire-les-reseaux-sociaux-aux-jeunes-selon-un-sondage", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "tech"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A large majority of people in Switzerland — 87% — would support banning social media for minors, according to a survey of 8,317 people conducted in August and reported this week. [single-source]. Support was high in both French- and German-speaking Switzerland, driven largely by concern over the mental-health risks the platforms pose to young people, per the poll carried out for Watson and relayed by Le Temps.", "why": "it signals broad public appetite for restrictions as several European governments weigh age limits on social platforms — even though no federal proposal for such a ban is on the table in Switzerland yet.", "thread_id": "2026-09-09-news-87-of-swiss-back-youth-social-media-ban", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-09", "event_date": "2026-09-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland"]}
{"id": "2026-09-09-news-explosion-at-ticino-power-plant", "date": "2026-09-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Explosion at Ticino power plant", "summary": "A large rescue operation followed an explosion at a power plant near Quinto in Ticino, with a possible partial building collapse reported.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/grosseinsatz-der-polizei-explosion-in-kraftwerk-bei-quinto-ti", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A large rescue operation was under way in Ticino after an explosion at a power plant near Quinto, in the Leventina valley, SRF reported on Wednesday 9 September. [single-source]. Fire crews, paramedics and a Rega rescue helicopter responded and police sealed off the area; SRF, citing the Ticino outlet tio.ch and RescueMedia, said part of the building may have collapsed and several people may have been affected, but that it was not yet clear in which building the blast occurred or how many people were hurt.", "why": "an explosion at an energy facility in the Gotthard region would be a rare industrial-safety incident, but the details so far are preliminary and have not been confirmed by the cantonal authorities.", "thread_id": "2026-09-09-news-explosion-at-ticino-power-plant", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-09", "event_date": "2026-09-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "Ticino", "Quinto"]}
